{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/37558-needing-help-for-a-scenario-the-new-gods-of-the-world","id":37558,"title":"Needing help for a scenario >.<, The New Gods of the World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T16:48:15-08:00","id":37558,"title":"Needing help for a scenario >.<, The New Gods of the World?","content":"Hello everyone. Christmas passed and a friend got me Scion heroes.. funny enough my Ex told him that &quot;I had a thing for mythology&quot; which she was wrong about xD.. Im starting to read the book of Scion Heroes and i started to work out an idea for a campain (Based on what my ex told to my friend)..You See, im a HUGE FAN of Neil Gaiman and the whole idea of American Gods, The battle between the old gods vs the contemporany ones its something that gives me a nerdgasm....but i was thinking on Which Gods would you create for a setting based on the God Wars? other than the ones on the basic book...Does anyone has a Pantheon of Contemporany Gods,or advices as for their powers, rules and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T22:24:56-08:00","id":37707,"title":"","content":"Well in my opinion I like the Godwar/God Politics Angle more then the Titanwar. It seems far less forced. There are a number of routes to go with to do contemporary Gods. So you have things like Nationalistic Pantheons, Pantheons that are just 2nd generations of other Pantheons forming Pantheons of their own, and Modern Pantheons based around things like God of the Internet, and God of Films and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:54:54-08:00","id":38107,"title":"","content":"Generally, I'd assume gods of modern concepts would by and large be Scions who took those positions, largely to not step on the toes of their divine parents.<br /> <br /> Of course if you're interested in conflicts between the Ancient Pantheons with no common enemy, I'd suggest looking at their own mythos. For instance, I'm pretty sure the Olympians don't care much for human sacrifice, which could put them at odds with the Aztec gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:36:57-08:00","id":38168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/37558-needing-help-for-a-scenario-the-new-gods-of-the-world?p=38107#post38107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course if you're interested in conflicts between the Ancient Pantheons with no common enemy, I'd suggest looking at their own mythos. For instance, I'm pretty sure the Olympians don't care much for human sacrifice, which could put them at odds with the Aztec gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, the Greeks performed human sacrifice. Not a lot, but it happened on occasion.<br /> <br /> Same goes for the Romans, though there are remnants of human sacrifice in some of their rituals. For example, captive leaders marching in triumphs sometimes ended up being executed at the end, while gladiatorial combat is thought to have started as fights to the death in honor of the deceased at funerals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T03:26:18-08:00","id":38657,"title":"","content":"You don't need to create new Gods. There are still polytheists nowadays such as the Taoists who believe in Hindu/Chinese gods and Indians worship Hindu Gods. They are not new, I give you that but they can't be considered ancient so... if you DO need a new Pantheon for western civilization it would be Wiccan Gods or simply Christianism which is Ancient pantheons worst enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}